{"id":"NCT06297291","title":"Global Paradise System US Post Approval Study","official":"The Global Paradise® System US Post Approval Study (US GPS)","summary":"The objective of the Global Paradise® System US Post Approval Study (US GPS) is to evaluate the real-world use of the Paradise Ultrasound Renal Denervation System indicated for patients who are unable to lower their blood pressure with lifestyle changes and medication. This system is comprised of a catheter, cable, balloon, and generator and has received FDA approval in the United States. Information collected in this study will be analyzed to better understand the long-term safety and effectiveness of treatment with the Paradise System for patients with high blood pressure.","conditions":["Hypertension","Cardiovascular Diseases","Vascular Diseases"],"interventions":[{"type":"DEVICE","name":"Paradise Ultrasound Renal Denervation Treatment"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Signed and dated study informed consent\n* Documented history of hypertension\n* Documented history of prior or current antihypertensive medication(s)\n* Baseline seated office systolic BP at screening ≥ 140 mmHg\n* Mean pre-procedure home systolic BP of ≥ 135 mmHg\n* Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) of ≥30 mL/min/m2\n\nRADIANCE CAP patients must provide signed and dated informed consent for inclusion in long-term follow-up. No other criteria are required for inclusion.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\nPatients who meet the following will be excluded from participation:\n\n* Subject under the age of 18 years old at the time of consent\n* Subject is pregnant prior to index procedure\\^ \\^ If a treated subject becomes pregnant after ultrasound RDN procedure, the subject will be followed for outcomes.\n\nThe ultrasound RDN procedure will be performed according to the IFU for the Paradise System and per the site's standard of care for interventional Procedures.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":1000,"start":"2024-06-28","pcd":"2028-12","upd":"2026-10-16","sponsor":"ReCor Medical, Inc.","areas":["other"],"central":["Helen Reeve-Stoffer, PhD · +1 650-912-9032 · hreeve-stoffer@recormedical.com","Liz Sheehan · Liz.Sheehan@recormedical.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Tibor Rubin VA Medical Center","city":"Long Beach","pr":"California","zip":"90822","s":"R","lat":33.767,"lon":-118.1892,"c":"Christine Ma · 562-826-8000 ext. 1-2889 · Christine.Agas@va.gov"},{"f":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90048","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Milagros Gonzalez · 424-315-0295 · milagros.gonzalez@cshs.org"},{"f":"Sutter Institute for Medical Research","city":"Sacramento","pr":"California","zip":"95816","s":"R","lat":38.5816,"lon":-121.4944,"c":"Kimberly Marinovich · Kimberly.Marinovich@sutterhealth.org"},{"f":"UC Davis Medical Center","city":"Sacramento","pr":"California","zip":"95817","s":"R","lat":38.5816,"lon":-121.4944,"c":"Cynthia O'Connell · 916-734-2197 · cloconnell@health.ucdavis.edu"},{"f":"Pacific Heart Institute","city":"Santa Monica","pr":"California","zip":"90404","s":"R","lat":34.0195,"lon":-118.4914,"c":"Alette Laughton · 424-315-4556 · research@pacificheart.com"},{"f":"Rocky Mountain Regional VAMC","city":"Aurora","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7294,"lon":-104.8319,"c":"David Korb · 720-857-5286 · David.Korb@va.gov"},{"f":"Medical Center of the Rockies","city":"Loveland","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80538","s":"R","lat":40.3978,"lon":-105.075,"c":"Tyler Lantvit · 970-624-1584 · Tyler.Lantvit@uchealth.org"},{"f":"Bridgeport Hosptial","city":"Bridgeport","pr":"Connecticut","zip":"06610","s":"R","lat":41.1792,"lon":-73.1894,"c":"Jessica LeBlanc · jessica.leblanc@bpthosp.org;"},{"f":"The Cardiac & Vascular Institute","city":"Gainesville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32605","s":"R","lat":29.6516,"lon":-82.3248,"c":"Marti Roberson · mroberson@tcavi.com"},{"f":"University of Miami 